            <ArticleTitle>MALDI-imaging enables direct observation of kinetic and thermodynamic products of mixed peptide fiber assembly.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1715-1718</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc10146a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Controlling the self-assembly of multicomponent systems provides a key to designing new materials and understanding the molecular complexity of biology. Here, we demonstrate the first use of MALDI-imaging to characterize a multicomponent self-assembling peptide fiber. Observations of mixed peptide systems over time demonstrate how simple sequence variation can change the balance between kinetic and thermodynamic products.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
